WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.770
Go get 'em, Zoro!

3
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.840
What are you waiting for?
Punch 'em out!

4
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.540
Knock them on the floor!
You can do it!

5
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.510
I don't need a cheering squad!
Go hide somewhere!

6
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.610
All right, you guys.

7
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.740
Do you think you could make this a little challenging?

8
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.400
Come on, Zoro!
This is why we keep you around!

9
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.440
It's the only thing you can do well, right?

10
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.380
Hurry up and finish
off those ugly-looking,

11
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.930
really bad, evil people...?

12
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.380
What do you think you're doing?
Hold up.

13
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.540
The primary rule
to assassination

14
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.490
says all weaker targets
are to be eliminated first.

15
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.610
We'll show you how professionals
handle these sorts of things.

16
00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.650
What, you mean me?

17
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.340
Hold on just a minute.

18
00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.970
Getting rid of me won't
accomplish anything at all.

19
00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:06.010
Sure, I'm pretty,
and I know how to dress.

20
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.980
But that's it. I really don't
have any fighting skills.

21
00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:12.650
Yes, we know.
It's fairly obvious.

22
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.880
As we said, picking off
the weak ones first

23
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.650
is the fastest way to work.

24
00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.810
And that's exactly
why I told her to shut up

25
00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.210
and hide somewhere.

26
00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:21.010
<b>She Who Controls the Weather</b>

27
00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.710
Luffy dead? Impossible!

28
00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.210
I don't believe you!

29
00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.450
Nonetheless, it's true.

30
00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.210
Poor Straw Hat, buried in
the sands of Rainbase,

31
00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:38.450
dear Miss Wednesday.

32
00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:42.000
If only he hadn't gotten
involved with you;

33
00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.950
he might've lived
a long and happy life.

34
00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.390
You're a liar!

35
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.300
He couldn't be killed by the likes of you!

36
00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.430
You know, it's only
because of his sacrifice

37
00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.900
that you're still alive to rave
and rant at this moment.

38
00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.300
You owe him your deepest thanks.

39
00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:02.140
That way, maybe he'll at least be able to...

40
00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.400
Tell me where he is!

41
00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:07.410
Did you come here
just to torture me?

42
00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.040
...be able to rest in peace.

43
00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:19.450
<b>Medi Assembly Hall
Alubarna North Block</b>

44
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.040
That brainless little fool,

45
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.680
where did she manage to
lose herself this time?

46
00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:19.880
This is why I told her to pipe
down and hide, but no!

47
00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.350
She has to go running off on her own

48
00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.080
and make me waste time
looking for her.

49
00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.020
Stupid Nami!

50
00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.990
That's it! I can't run anymore!

51
00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.060
I'll have to fight!

52
00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.890
Like hell!

53
00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:46.230
This is taking too long.

54
00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.130
So hasty.

55
00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.800
Zoro!

56
00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.580
That stone column just split into pieces!

57
00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:09.580
<b>Roronoa Zoro and Nami</b>
<b>Mr. 1 and Miss Doublefinger</b>
<b>vs</b>

58
00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.050
It didn't split.

59
00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:09.910
It was sliced.

60
00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.550
Only a swordsman could've
done something like that.

61
00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.710
That's right.

62
00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.720
You cut it, didn't you?

63
00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.820
With those arms, huh?

64
00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:30.080
You've got a rather unusual body, don't you?

65
00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.330
You noticed.

66
00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.840
I ate the Dice Dice Fruit,
making blades of my entire body.

67
00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.070
You're him.

68
00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.870
The swordsman who
supposedly cut down

69
00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:41.710
a hundred men at Whiskey Peak.

70
00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:42.880
He's also the pirate

71
00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.880
who turned down an invitation
to join Baroque Works

72
00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.850
several years ago at East Blue,

73
00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:50.020
and cut down our
Mr. 7 at the time.

74
00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:51.350
That was you too?

75
00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.560
Ha! That's a story
that takes me back.

76
00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.070
That little misunderstanding
was your Mr. 7's fault

77
00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.940
for not accepting the
terms I offered him.

78
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.100
As I remember it, I made a very generous proposition.

79
00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:07.010
I said, "Sure, I'll join, as
long as you make me your boss."

80
00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.340
You're quite a comedian, aren't you?

81
00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:11.940
Instead of meeting my terms,

82
00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:13.780
he rather rudely took
a slash at me,

83
00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:16.850
so naturally, I put
him in his place.

84
00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:19.150
Now would you like to invite me too?

85
00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.050
'Cause right now, you guys
look so ridiculous,

86
00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:24.880
I wouldn't even accept the job.

87
00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.790
You think you can make a fool out of me?

88
00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.930
You, some swordsman from
an upstart pirate crew?

89
00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.130
Maybe I am, but what
do you think you guys are?

90
00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.400
Puppets with no
will of your own

91
00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:46.910
being manipulated by Crocodile
into building his fake utopia.

92
00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:50.130
Or maybe you're all just little tin soldiers.

93
00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.710
All shine and no steel.

94
00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.150
Miss Doublefinger.

95
00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:00.350
I know, I know, you want to
eliminate him, don't you?

96
00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:04.660
You do as you please.
I'll take care of the girl.

97
00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.730
Uh! Nami, be careful...
Okay... she's gone.

98
00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.290
I guess her plan must've failed.

99
00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:33.460
She wasn't able to stop the rebel army at the entrance.

100
00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:37.900
I wonder if Vivi and
the others are all right.

101
00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:42.400
They're all fighting, putting
their lives on the line...

102
00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:45.220
...and here I am
running and hiding.

103
00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.470
You heard me! I need help!

104
00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.970
I want you to build me a weapon!

105
00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.890
Build you a weapon?

106
00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.400
And what are you gonna do
with it, hide behind it?

107
00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:01.380
Touché.

108
00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.150
Okay, so I'm not a warrior.

109
00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.820
I'm just really cute with a great figure.

110
00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:06.820
Say what?

111
00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.960
But even so...

112
00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:11.360
I at least wanna
be strong enough

113
00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.070
not to endanger the others.

114
00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:17.370
Especially this time. For Vivi.

115
00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:41.450
Usopp, I know you understand how I feel.

116
00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.920
We're not like the others.

117
00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:58.430
<b>iUYjRFTECw SyrdeNQOmY gWKZbsxDEX hnOSJNHoOT YDZLTnBrny KoJXxnJOIX</b>
<b>eoHmvxeIBt</b>
<b>RDKUjcbNnW</b>

118
00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:48.160
They're all as strong as monsters.

119
00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:50.260
In a fight, they can
rely on their own power

120
00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.360
to defeat almost any enemy.

121
00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:55.360
But us, we're just a couple
of ordinary humans

122
00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:57.480
with no special abilities.

123
00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:02.110
When a battle starts, you and I are just in the way.

124
00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:06.420
We're a burden to the others;
we can't even protect ourselves.

125
00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:11.060
If we're gonna fight beside them, we need weapons.

126
00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:12.960
Really powerful ones.

127
00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.430
Or else...

128
00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.070
Isn't that the
reason you're always

129
00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.450
inventing new weapons?

130
00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:25.320
So you'll be able to hold
your own in a battle

131
00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:26.640
with them without shame?

132
00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.400
Am I right?

133
00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.140
It's the same for me!

134
00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:36.510
To help Vivi, I wanna fight
with my own two hands!

135
00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:38.360
Will you help me or not?

136
00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.000
We don't have much time
left till we reach Alabasta.

137
00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.930
You're right.

138
00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:51.140
I guess you can't turn me into a warrior overnight.

139
00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:54.010
Sorry for being so unreasonable.

140
00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:57.280
Unreasonable, maybe,
but it's not impossible.

141
00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:01.450
Hey, were you suggesting
there's something

142
00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.120
the mighty Usopp can't do?

143
00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:05.190
Yeah?

144
00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:14.510
<b>iUYjRFTECw SyrdeNQOmY gWKZbsxDEX hnOSJNHoOT YDZLTnBrny KoJXxnJOIX</b>
<b>eoHmvxeIBt</b>
<b>RDKUjcbNnW</b>

145
00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.240
Does that mean
you're really gonna do it?

146
00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.710
I love you! Thank you, Usopp!

147
00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.750
Now, as to the matter of
the cost, this won't be...

148
00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.060
I really, really
mean it, thank you!

149
00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:17.220
Yeah, we covered the gratitude part.

150
00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.520
But top-of-the-line
weapons aren't free.

151
00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:19.790
I'm counting on you, 'kay?

152
00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:21.750
Hold on a minute!

153
00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:24.790
Relax, boys,
you're off the hook.

154
00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:26.220
– Hm?
– Hm?

155
00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:28.430
But, Nami...

156
00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:40.770
What am I doing?

157
00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:43.740
I'm jumping at noises now.

158
00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:47.200
And after I shot my mouth off

159
00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:49.440
in front of Usopp like that.

160
00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:54.480
I'm ready, aren't I?
To fight for Vivi?

161
00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:06.090
After all,
Usopp kept his promise.

162
00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.920
Okay, I'll fight!

163
00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.920
If it's just that one woman,
I should be able to...

164
00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:38.610
Give it up, girl. It's useless.

165
00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.500
Miss Doublefinger!

166
00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:43.450
But what was that spear-like
weapon she used?

167
00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:47.180
Does she have Devil
Fruit powers too?

168
00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:49.410
I know what you're thinking.

169
00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.650
You're right. I ate
the Spike Spike Fruit.

170
00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:55.550
It granted me the power
to release spikes

171
00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:57.420
from anywhere on my body.

172
00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:58.400
Spikes that can pierce

173
00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.470
right through a
solid stone wall!

174
00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.280
If I slip up just once, she'll
make a pincushion out of me,

175
00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.310
and that'll be the
end of the story!

176
00:12:05.310 --> 00:12:06.480
What?

177
00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:09.510
Don't tell me you're actually going to try and fight me!

178
00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:10.980
Yes!

179
00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.020
It can call upon clouds.

180
00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:18.160
It can summon forth the rain.

181
00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.630
It can create the wind itself!

182
00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:23.230
My marvelous invention
can cause disaster

183
00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.640
with its elemental power!

184
00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:31.120
Stay away, or feel the
force of my Clima Takt!

185
00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.320
Clima? What now?

186
00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.650
First, sunny weather!

187
00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:37.180
Fine Tempo!

188
00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:38.940
Uhh...

189
00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.910
Wow, look at that!
It made doves appear!

190
00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:45.540
Dumb thing!

191
00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:53.720
Are you all right?

192
00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.750
Okay, that was
just the first try!

193
00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:58.520
Besides, now we've gotten
her to lower her guard.

194
00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:01.220
Very clever, Usopp!

195
00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.560
This time you've had it!

196
00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:05.030
Cloudy Tempo!

197
00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:08.060
And now we've got some pretty flowers!

198
00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:19.880
I don't know
her story, but what a poor kid!

199
00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:24.460
Try again! Save the princess!

200
00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:26.430
Cannons! Bring cannons in!

201
00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:27.530
Destroy the gate!

202
00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:29.330
Hurry!

203
00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:35.340
Dieciseis Fleurs!

204
00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:44.380
What the...?

205
00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.930
Maybe now we can have a little peace and quiet.

206
00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:44.100
What a stubborn girl.

207
00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:50.800
You're just wasting your time dodging my attacks.

208
00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.940
You know you haven't got a chance.

209
00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:54.940
I do too!

210
00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:58.610
These instructions say there are tons more attacks to try!

211
00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.450
Now be a good girl and stay right where you are.

212
00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:05.950
That way I'll be able to kill you

213
00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:09.420
without causing you too much pain.

214
00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:14.430
Aw, does this show of yours have a second act?

215
00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.330
Forecast: Thunder!

216
00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:18.880
Thunder Tempo!

217
00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:28.390
Thunder Tempo...

218
00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:30.420
Thunder Tempo. Thunder...

219
00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.490
Finger... Stinger!

220
00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:48.870
Eh.

221
00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:54.440
My cheek is bleeding.

222
00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.110
Am I gonna die like this?

223
00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:01.520
I am, aren't I? I'm gonna die.

224
00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:02.880
And I'll haunt him!

225
00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.090
Long-nosed fool!
Long-nosed fool!

226
00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:09.760
Long-nosed... Why didn't
he make a real weapon?!

227
00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.530
What's this?

228
00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:16.930
So, I'll kill you now, okay?

229
00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:28.640
How is she doing that? And why?

230
00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:34.440
Hedgehog Stinger!

231
00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:35.940
Too close!

232
00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.710
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa! Wait!

233
00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:39.970
Hold on!

234
00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:40.990
I said hold on! Just a minute!
Can't you give a girl a minute?

235
00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:45.060
I'm not ready yet!
Come on! Cease fire!

236
00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:47.510
No fair! Time out! Stop!

237
00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:50.100
I can't stay out
in the open like this!

238
00:16:58.570 --> 00:16:59.630
This is it!

239
00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:01.530
Time for you to get skewered!

240
00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:03.140
No...

241
00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:04.700
...thank you!

242
00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:19.220
Well...

243
00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:23.620
It looks like she's got a
little more battle experience

244
00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:25.090
than I thought.

245
00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.630
Not that it'll help.

246
00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:28.160
Where was it?

247
00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:30.790
I saw it.

248
00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.970
There was something
that looked useful

249
00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:35.670
somewhere in these
Clima Takt instructions.

250
00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.200
Dammit, where?

251
00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:38.300
That's it!

252
00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:39.910
Next time you're at a party and things are slow,

253
00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.810
just use these little
tricks I've written up

254
00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.620
and things'll really
start to jump!

255
00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:45.740
People will love 'em!

256
00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.020
I'll kill you!

257
00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:52.220
Oh, by the way,

258
00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:55.290
I've jotted down a few battle
configurations on the back.

259
00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.100
On the back?

260
00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:01.920
Hm?

261
00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.910
Let's see, where could you

262
00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:09.880
be hiding yourself this
time, little kitty?

263
00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:19.240
I'm through running and hiding!

264
00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:22.300
I may not look it, but during my eight years as a thief,

265
00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:27.080
I survived all kinds of
crises all by myself!

266
00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:31.250
You can't treat me like some ordinary girl.

267
00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:33.420
Now bring it on, hussy!

268
00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:36.750
My, my. Kitty found her claws.

269
00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:39.360
Well, then. Show me
what you've got.

270
00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:43.060
You got it! Taste my real power!

271
00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:44.220
The battle configurations

272
00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.350
of the Clima Takt!

273
00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.920
First, understand the
characteristics of each section!

274
00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:50.940
Each one can shoot
off air bubbles,

275
00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:54.030
either by shaking or blowing!

276
00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:56.240
The first shoots hot air.

277
00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:01.000
Heat Ball!

278
00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:03.250
What's this? It's warm.

279
00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.620
Next shoots cool air.

280
00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.870
Cool Ball!

281
00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:10.940
Ah, how pleasant.

282
00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.610
The last shoots electricity.

283
00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:17.120
Thunder Ball!

284
00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:19.050
Oh, my, that tingled!

285
00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.150
Of course, these techniques

286
00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.290
aren't quite finished yet,

287
00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:24.130
so if you use 'em at parties,
you need to be careful.

288
00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.000
Then why write 'em down?!

289
00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.670
Look, are we done here?

290
00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:35.740
Sewing Stinger!

291
00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.640
Please, please, something
I can use for battle.

292
00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:39.340
Not for parties,
some real techniques,

293
00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:41.180
something I can fight with!

294
00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:51.160
I'm sorry, girl, but I've
had enough of these games.

295
00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.990
Stinger Step!

296
00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.820
I see! The Heat Ball and
Cool Ball join together!

297
00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.160
When they stop spinning,

298
00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.860
the bubbles hit each other,
creating an air flow,

299
00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:17.130
generating a powerful wind!

300
00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.760
Brilliant, Usopp!

301
00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:21.030
The Cyclone Tempo is
like an ordinary boomerang,

302
00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:23.250
so if you take it outside
after the party to play with,

303
00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:24.420
you have to watch out.

304
00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:27.420
He really doesn't get it.

305
00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:29.560
But let's see here...

306
00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:31.120
Maybe I...

307
00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.200
What kind of weapon is that?

308
00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:39.410
Don't you dare turn
your back on me!

309
00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:44.410
To turn your back to your enemy
in the middle of a battle...

310
00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:47.410
You didn't value your life too highly.

311
00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:03.500
I changed the air density
by using a Cool Ball.

312
00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:06.270
The temperature difference
caused a refraction of light

313
00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:07.430
known as...

314
00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:08.840
A mirage!

315
00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:12.170
No way. At this distance?

316
00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.340
We can't win with power.

317
00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:21.350
If we're gonna survive,
we gotta use our brains!

318
00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:25.480
Heh. That's how we fight, right?

319
00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:28.490
Used properly, this can make miracles.

320
00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:30.860
I'd say this is the perfect weapon for me.

321
00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:37.730
Okay, Spiky. I'm ready.

322
00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:39.900
Now why don't you give up?

323
00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:43.320
<b>Southeast Gate, Alubarna</b>

324
00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:46.180
Huh.

325
00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:48.180
Well, well. You're alive.

326
00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:48.980
Huh?

327
00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:49.650
Oh, man.

328
00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:51.180
– Sanji!
– Sanji!

329
00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:52.980
You're hurt!

330
00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:57.390
So, does this mean
that you beat up Mr. 2?

331
00:21:57.400 --> 00:21:59.440
Better believe it!

332
00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:00.790
Here.

333
00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:02.500
My-My goggles!

334
00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:04.690
So you got 'em back for me
from that creep, huh?

335
00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:07.530
Thank you, Sanji!
Oh, you're the best!

336
00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:09.050
Wait a minute. They're broken!

337
00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:11.450
In that case, I take back everything I said!

338
00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:12.770
Thanks for nothin', ya jerk!

339
00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:14.580
And they were the
latest models too!

340
00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:17.050
Do you have any idea what I had
to do to get these things?

341
00:22:17.070 --> 00:22:18.100
Hey, look at that.

342
00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:20.170
Look at my poor goggles.

343
00:22:20.210 --> 00:22:21.620
Whoa!

344
00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:23.030
That must be the auxiliary force

345
00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:24.970
for the rebel army.

346
00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:26.810
There's more of them?

347
00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:27.980
Looks like it.

348
00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:32.220
I guess Vivi wasn't able to stop the fighting in time.

349
00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:33.550
This is just great!

350
00:22:34.210 --> 00:22:36.380
Eh? What the hell?

351
00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:38.760
Hey! Eyelash! It's about
time you showed up!

352
00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:39.790
Where've you been hiding?

353
00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:40.930
Let's hurry to the palace.

354
00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:43.650
Maybe there's still a way we can help Vivi out.

355
00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:44.590
Come on!

356
00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:45.420
Right!

357
00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:46.660
Usopp, move it!

358
00:22:46.690 --> 00:22:48.160
I'm coming! I'm coming!

359
00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:49.990
Hey, Eyelash, gimme a lift!

360
00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:51.830
Wait! Stop! Don'tcha
see the bandages?

361
00:22:51.860 --> 00:22:54.000
Help an injured
man out, would ya?

362
00:22:55.870 --> 00:22:57.370
No, Father!

363
00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:04.410
Let the king go,
Crocodile! At once!

364
00:23:05.750 --> 00:23:08.360
Vivi, I'm sorry.

365
00:23:08.390 --> 00:23:11.230
I failed you and the nation.

366
00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:15.100
I didn't use the chance you risked your life for.

367
00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:17.070
Oh, Father.

368
00:23:23.220 --> 00:23:25.190
Let me tell you a little something.

369
00:23:25.220 --> 00:23:29.020
I have no intention of keeping
you or your father alive.

370
00:23:29.060 --> 00:23:30.290
When a kingdom dies out,

371
00:23:30.290 --> 00:23:34.800
it only seems natural its royal
family should die out as well.

372
00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:38.580
But first, before I take the throne,

373
00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:41.150
there's something I need to ask the current king.

374
00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:43.820
If you have a moment, that is.

375
00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:50.820
In fact, this has been my goal from the very beginning.

376
00:23:51.590 --> 00:23:55.860
Cobra, tell me, where's the Pluton?

377
00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:10.180
How can... you know that name?
